#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Portfolio builder: maximize model upside with portfolio β kept in 0.5–1.25.

Universe = eligible famous household names (≥20% upside) + all FvIndustries names with model upside ≥ 35%
(beta, upside, price, FV from refreshed industry JSON files).

Modes:
  1) Full auto — optimize weights across the whole universe:
       python3 Builder

  2) You pick 1–4 anchors from the famous stocks; Builder auto-fills to 12 total (picks + auto):
       python3 Builder --pick IBM UBER DIS
       python3 Builder --pick JPM MA V --size 12
       python3 Builder --list-famous

Pick mode: choose 1–4 from ``FAMOUS_STOCKS`` (≥20% upside); auto-fill rest from ≥35% universe.
Your picks capped at 10% each; auto-fill gets 5–10% by Sharpe (≥1 → 8–10%, <1 → 5–8%) with β in 0.5–1.25.
Auto names stay at least 3% below pick weight. Up to 12 names total (your picks + auto-fill); uses only as many as needed.
"""

